1. DEFINITIONS
1.1. "Program" means Platform_ppi_docking: the source code in this repository, the packages and container
     images published by the Author, the documentation and the configuration files that
     accompany them.
1.2. "Author" means Luiz Dione Barbosa De-Melo, who holds the rights to the Program.
1.3. "Personal use" means use by a natural person, on their own equipment, with no economic
     purpose and without providing a service to third parties.
1.4. "Use in teaching" means use in teaching and learning activities — classes, courses,
     training, workshops and demonstrations — by educational institutions and by their students
     and faculty, including use by a student in coursework.
1.5. "Use in research" means use that generates, processes or analyses data intended for
     scientific investigation, including in a dissertation, thesis, research report, funding
     application, preprint, article, abstract, poster, conference presentation or patent.
1.6. "Commercial use" means use aimed, directly or indirectly, at economic gain, such as paid
     services, consulting, analysis performed for a client, sale, rental, sublicensing, offering
     as a service (SaaS), and use in business activity.

2. FREE USES
2.1. The Author grants a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide, non-transferable and revocable
     licence to download, install, run and read the Program for Personal use and for Use in
     teaching, provided the authorship notices and this licence are kept.
2.2. These uses require no prior notice to the Author.

3. USE IN RESEARCH — REQUIRES PRIOR AUTHORIZATION
3.1. Use in research is permitted only after PRIOR, EXPRESS AUTHORIZATION from the Author,
     requested by e-mail to luiz.melo@ifrj.edu.br.
3.2. The request must state who will use the Program, the institution, the purpose of the
     research and the intended destination of the results.
3.3. The authorization is personal, limited to the project described in the request, and does
     not extend to other projects, groups or institutions. The Author may grant, deny or
     condition it, including on forms of authorship credit, and may revoke it for breach of this
     licence.
3.4. Running the Program only to learn about or evaluate it, without generating research data or
     results, is Personal use and requires no authorization.

4. COMMERCIAL USE
4.1. Commercial use is not permitted under this licence, under any circumstances.
4.2. Those interested should contact the Author to negotiate a specific licence.

5. GENERAL LIMITS
5.1. Without the Author's written authorization, it is prohibited to: distribute copies of the
     Program, in whole or in part; publish it in another repository, registry or application
     store; modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works; reverse engineer it, except as
